  "title": "Three-fold spaces are an Euler count: easy for Sherali-Adams, only treewidth-bounded for resolution",
  "subject": "The global proof complexity of the knot's three-fold spaces",
  "conclusion": "Refutations of three-fold spaces compose over the handle tree at constant cost per Fano piece, and on a plane core the contradiction is Euler's count of two more faces than lines, which Sherali-Adams of level three refutes. Resolution gets only the treewidth bound 2^O(sqrt n), and solver costs on the octahedral family grow exponentially in sqrt n, so the two-round rule does not compose into a global resolution bound.",
